hile, experts said the country is headed for a budget crisis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tesla planning €3BN investment in German factory to produce Cybercabs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd0f23821059ed0086dd03dfa6352701075b8b56e65b9a2b10be536fe46e7c89</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tesla-planning-_3bn-investment-in-german-factory-to-produce-cybercabs/a-79961416--56a989627169.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tesla-planning-€3bn-investment-in-german-factory-to-produce-cybercabs/a-79961416?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Elon Musk-owned company is looking to further expand its only European production line. Brandenburg's state leader has welcomed the decision.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The AfD and neo-Nazi networks: how close are the connections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32d484b124507f057f26b2733e88aa17f1e96b26f74827cdefb90d1ba47e8853</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:42:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-afd-and-neo-nazi-networks-how-close-are-the-connections/a-79961920--fb16f5d74381.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-afd-and-neo-nazi-networks-how-close-are-the-connections/a-79961920?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party (AfD) has become a focal point for the far right. Many of its members and staff have ties to ethnonationalist or neo-Nazi organizations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Infantino out as FIFA candidate deadline looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbb7c6c46a17bd745de97024d29acbb76b8c6752a403c112d0ae661cbe6cb874</id><updated>2026-11-16T18:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href=